  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Interactive Visual Lab 1: Rotary Position Embeddings (RoPE)\n",
    "\n",
    "Welcome! In this interactive notebook, we will visualize how **RoPE (Rotary Position Embeddings)** works using **interactive matplotlib animations, live sliders, and runnable PyTorch code**.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Setup & Environment\n",
    "Let's import our dependencies and ensure the project path is linked."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "root_dir = Path.cwd().parent if Path.cwd().name == 'notebooks' else Path.cwd()\n",
    "if str(root_dir) not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.insert(0, str(root_dir))\n",
    "\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from ipywidgets import interact, IntSlider, Output\n",
    "from IPython.display import display, Markdown\n",
    "\n",
    "from src.model.rope import precompute_freqs_cis, apply_rotary_emb\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set high-DPI clean dark/light styling\n",
    "plt.rcParams['figure.dpi'] = 110\n",
    "plt.rcParams['font.size'] = 10\n",
    "print(\"Interactive libraries loaded successfully!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 2. Interactive Clock Visualizer (Live Sliders)\n",
    "\n",
    "### The Math\n",
    "Every position step rotates the vector by an angle $\\theta$:\n",
    "$$\\mathbf{q}_m = \\mathbf{R}(m \\cdot \\theta) \\mathbf{q}$$\n",
    "$$\\mathbf{k}_n = \\mathbf{R}(n \\cdot \\theta) \\mathbf{k}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The attention dot product between them is:\n",
    "$$\\mathbf{q}_m^\\top \\mathbf{k}_n = \\cos((n - m) \\cdot \\theta)$$\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Try this in the widget below:**\n",
    "> 1. Set $m = 10$ and $n = 12$ (Distance = $2$). Note the angle and score.\n",
    "> 2. Now slide both up to $m = 40$ and $n = 42$ (Distance is still $2$).\n",
    "> 3. Watch the hands spin, but observe that the **angle difference and the score stay identical!**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def plot_rope_clock(pos_m=10, pos_n=12, step_deg=30):\n",
    "    fig, (ax_clock, ax_wave) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(11, 5.2))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # --- 1. CLOCK FACE ---\n",
    "    circle = plt.Circle((0, 0), 1.0, color='#30363d', fill=False, linewidth=2, linestyle='--')\n",
    "    ax_clock.add_artist(circle)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Hour ticks\n",
    "    for i in range(12):\n",
    "        deg = i * 30\n",
    "        rad = np.radians(deg)\n",
    "        ax_clock.plot([0.9 * np.sin(rad), np.sin(rad)], [0.9 * np.cos(rad), np.cos(rad)], color='#8b949e', lw=1.5)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Angles in radians (0 at 12 o'clock, clockwise)\n",
    "    angle_m_rad = np.radians((pos_m * step_deg) % 360)\n",
    "    angle_n_rad = np.radians((pos_n * step_deg) % 360)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Coordinates for hands (0 deg = (0, 1))\n",
    "    xm, ym = 0.85 * np.sin(angle_m_rad), 0.85 * np.cos(angle_m_rad)\n",
    "    xn, yn = 0.70 * np.sin(angle_n_rad), 0.70 * np.cos(angle_n_rad)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Draw hands\n",
    "    ax_clock.annotate('', xy=(xm, ym), xytext=(0, 0),\n",
    "                      arrowprops=dict(facecolor='#58a6ff', edgecolor='#1f6feb', width=3, headwidth=10))\n",
    "    ax_clock.annotate('', xy=(xn, yn), xytext=(0, 0),\n",
    "                      arrowprops=dict(facecolor='#bc8cff', edgecolor='#8957e5', width=3, headwidth=10))\n",
    "    ax_clock.plot(0, 0, 'o', color='#ffffff', markersize=6)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Formatting clock\n",
    "    ax_clock.set_xlim(-1.25, 1.25)\n",
    "    ax_clock.set_ylim(-1.25, 1.25)\n",
    "    ax_clock.set_aspect('equal')\n",
    "    ax_clock.axis('off')\n",
    "    ax_clock.set_title(\"2D RoPE Rotation Clock Face\", fontsize=12, fontweight='bold', pad=12)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Legend\n",
    "    ax_clock.text(0, -1.2, f\"Blue: Query pos {pos_m} | Purple: Key pos {pos_n}\", \n",
    "                  ha='center', fontsize=10, bbox=dict(boxstyle='round,pad=0.4', facecolor='#161b22', edgecolor='#30363d'))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # --- 2. ATTENTION SCORE VS RELATIVE DISTANCE ---\n",
    "    distances = np.arange(0, 25)\n",
    "    scores = np.cos(np.radians(distances * step_deg))\n",
    "    cur_dist = abs(pos_n - pos_m)\n",
    "    cur_score = np.cos(np.radians(cur_dist * step_deg))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    ax_wave.plot(distances, scores, color='#58a6ff', lw=2, label=r'Theoretical $\cos(\Delta \cdot \\theta)$')\n",
    "    ax_wave.axhline(0, color='#8b949e', linestyle=':', alpha=0.6)\n",
    "    ax_wave.plot(cur_dist, cur_score, 'ro', markersize=9, label=f'Current Dist = {cur_dist}')\n",
    "    ax_wave.set_title(\"Attention Score vs Relative Distance (n - m)\", fontsize=12, fontweight='bold', pad=12)\n",
    "    ax_wave.set_xlabel(\"Relative Token Distance |n - m|\", fontsize=10)\n",
    "    ax_wave.set_ylabel(\"Attention Dot Product Score\", fontsize=10)\n",
    "    ax_wave.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "    ax_wave.legend(loc='upper right')\n",
    "    \n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Display live Markdown metrics below plot\n",
    "    deg_diff = (cur_dist * step_deg) % 360\n",
    "    display(Markdown(f\"\"\"\n",
    "> ### Live Status\n",
    "> - **Relative Distance:** `{cur_dist}` tokens\n",
    "> - **Angular Difference:** `{deg_diff:.1f}°`\n",
    "> - **Attention Score:** `{cur_score:.4f}`\n",
    "> \n",
    "> *(Notice: Even if you slide both $m$ and $n$ across the entire context, as long as $|n - m|$ remains constant, the score is invariant!)*\n",
    "\"\"\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create interactive sliders widget\n",
    "interact(\n",
    "    plot_rope_clock,\n",
    "    pos_m=IntSlider(min=0, max=60, step=1, value=10, description='Query (m):'),\n",
    "    pos_n=IntSlider(min=0, max=60, step=1, value=12, description='Key (n):'),\n",
    "    step_deg=IntSlider(min=10, max=90, step=5, value=30, description='Angle Step (°):')\n",
    ");"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 3. Real PyTorch Verification (Under the Hood)\n",
    "\n",
    "Now let's verify that the PyTorch tensors produced by `src/model/rope.py` give the exact same result as our visual clock!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Precompute frequency tables for head_dim = 64\n",
    "head_dim = 64\n",
    "max_seq_len = 256\n",
    "cos, sin = precompute_freqs_cis(dim=head_dim, max_seq_len=max_seq_len)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sample query and key vectors for 'def' and 'quicksort'\n",
    "torch.manual_seed(42)\n",
    "q = torch.randn(1, 1, 1, head_dim)\n",
    "k = torch.randn(1, 1, 1, head_dim)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test 1: Positions (10, 12)\n",
    "q10, _ = apply_rotary_emb(q, q, cos[10:11], sin[10:11])\n",
    "_, k12 = apply_rotary_emb(k, k, cos[12:13], sin[12:13])\n",
    "score_1 = (q10 * k12).sum().item()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Test 2: Shifted to (40, 42)\n",
    "q40, _ = apply_rotary_emb(q, q, cos[40:41], sin[40:41])\n",
    "_, k42 = apply_rotary_emb(k, k, cos[42:43], sin[42:43])\n",
    "score_2 = (q40 * k42).sum().item()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"PyTorch Dot Product at (10, 12): {score_1:.6f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"PyTorch Dot Product at (40, 42): {score_2:.6f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Absolute Difference:             {abs(score_1 - score_2):.10f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "assert abs(score_1 - score_2) < 1e-5\n",
    "print(\"\\nSUCCESS: PyTorch implementation matches mathematical invariance perfectly!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 4. Multi-Frequency Geometry: Why Dimensions Rotate at Different Speeds\n",
    "\n",
    "A single head vector doesn't just have 1 frequency—it has $d / 2$ pairs of frequencies!\n",
    "$$\\theta_i = \\text{base}^{-2i / d}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's plot how the rotation speed decays across the dimensions of a head vector:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "dim_indices = np.arange(0, head_dim, 2)\n",
    "theta_base = 10000.0\n",
    "frequencies = 1.0 / (theta_base ** (dim_indices / head_dim))\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 4))\n",
    "ax.plot(dim_indices, frequencies, 'o-', color='#3fb950', lw=2)\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"RoPE Frequency Decay Across Head Dimensions (d = 64)\", fontsize=11, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Head Dimension Coordinate Pair (2i)\", fontsize=10)\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(r\"Rotation Frequency $\\theta_i$\", fontsize=10)\n",
    "ax.set_yscale('log')\n",
    "ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.text(2, frequencies[1], \"Fast Rotation (Local Grammar & Syntax)\", \n",
    "        fontsize=9, color='#58a6ff', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "ax.text(28, frequencies[-2], \"Slow Rotation (Long-Range Global Context)\", \n",
    "        fontsize=9, color='#bc8cff', fontweight='bold')\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  }
 ],
